cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "qountstat: Statistical Analysis of Count Data and Quantal Data"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-16"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/YOUR-GITHUB-USERNAME/qountstat"
url: "https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=qountstat"
abstract: >-
  Methods for the statistical analysis of count data and quantal data in
  ecotoxicology. Implementations of the Closure Principle Computational
  Approach Test (CPCAT), of a Dunnett GLM approach with a quasi-Poisson,
  negative binomial or Poisson regression, and of the Closure Principle
  Fisher-Freeman-Halton test (CPFISH). P-values and no/lowest observed
  (adverse) effect concentration values are calculated. A model-agnostic,
  simulation-calibrated diagnostic for overdispersion is provided to
  support the choice between the implemented methods.
keywords:
  - ecotoxicology
  - count data
  - NOEC
  - overdispersion
  - R
authors:
